{"key": "e4747e7669e733487370e145901b4606", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "response": {"content": [{"text": "Part of this is covered: the passages have SIM chip setup steps, but nothing on Wi-Fi or signal.\n\n**Chip setup:**\n- With the machine off, open the cover on the back [2].\n- Insert the chip in the slot marked SIM1 or SIM2, with the metal side facing down [2].\n- Close the cover, turn the machine on, and wait for it to connect to the data network [2].\n- When it shows a connected network (2G or 3G), the machine is ready to use [2].\n- Then run a communication test to check that the chip is connecting. The passage cuts off before listing the test steps [2].\n\n**Manuals:** Getnet has downloadable user manuals for each machine type, including \"Portátil com Chip + Wi-Fi\", \"Chip de dados + Wi-Fi\" and Get Renova [4].\n\nThe passages don't cover Wi-Fi setup steps or what to do about a weak signal. They also don't give the communication test steps.\n\nAs for your ticket request, the assistant can propose opening a support ticket for a terminal, but nothing runs until you confirm [policy:capabilities]. If you want that, send me the terminal ID (format T0000A) [policy:capabilities].\n\nMISSING: Wi-Fi connection steps, signal troubleshooting, and the full communication test steps", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CggS2UjJQvGun3hHs7BCG", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3991, "output_tokens": 426, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}, "role": "agent", "scope": "approval-04#0"}
